# 🌺 श्रवण से स्थितप्रज्ञता तक — पूरी यात्रा

आचार्य जयप्रकाश जी की टिप्पणियों को एक सूत्र-माला में रखें तो अद्भुत क्रम दिखाई देता है:

**श्रवण**
→ **श्रद्धा और पात्रता**
→ **अहंकार की नम्रता**
→ **मोह का निरीक्षण**
→ **इन्द्रिय-संयम**
→ **विषय-चिन्तन की सजगता**
→ **संग और कामना की पहचान**
→ **राग–भय–क्रोध का क्षय**
→ **अन्तःकरण-प्रसाद**
→ **स्थिर बुद्धि**
→ **गुणा गुणेषु वर्तन्ते**
→ **अकर्तृत्व**
→ **स्वरूप में विश्रान्ति।**

अब स्पष्ट होता है—

### **ज्ञान सुनना आरम्भ है।

ज्ञान बनकर जीना परिपक्वता है।**

---

# 🌺 English Contemplation

## **Knowledge Needs a Prepared Heart**

Truth may be spoken clearly and still remain unheard.

The obstacle is not always lack of information.

Sometimes it is the inability to listen without defending what we already believe.

This is why the traditional idea of *adhikāra*—preparedness—is so important.

It does not mean spiritual superiority.

It means receptivity.

Can I listen?

Can I question?

Can I discover that my previous understanding was incomplete without feeling diminished?

Can insight survive when desire, anger, fear, praise, loss, and attachment enter daily life?

This is where knowledge becomes sādhana.

The Gītā's sequence is psychologically precise:

Repeated dwelling produces attachment.

Attachment becomes demand.

Obstructed demand becomes anger.

Anger clouds discernment.

Clouded discernment obscures remembrance.

And when remembrance of what truly matters is lost, intelligence no longer guides life clearly.

The movement toward steady wisdom therefore reverses this process.

Awareness replaces unconscious dwelling.

Non-attachment loosens demand.

Equanimity weakens reaction.

Inner clarity stabilizes understanding.

Eventually action continues, yet the burden—

**“I am the independent doer of all this”**

—begins to dissolve.

Then knowledge is no longer merely something we have heard.

### **It has begun to become the way we live.**

